m was hardly noticed. Plenty of other heroes were dying elsewhere. Plenty of bigger bits of history were being made.", "reference": "2022 January 12, Benedict le Vay, “The heroes of Soham...”, in RAIL, number 1948, page 43:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A role model.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "The protagonist in a work of fiction.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "However, even this great hero of the story is somewhat of a simpleton (when he lets himself be crucially deceived by Peacock Ravana in Vibhisana's shape), and a weakling (when in spite of all his strength he is almost beaten by his own son, one of the rākṣasas)", "reference": "1987, Kamil Zvelebil, Two Tamil Folktales: The Story of King Matan̲akāma, The Story of Peacock Rāvaṇa, →ISBN, page xlii:"}, {"text": "Satan is wrongly called the hero of Paradise Lost. He is really the villain-hero or the counter-hero", "reference": "1992, Karuna Shanker Mishra, The Tragic Hero Through the Ages, page 242:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(poker) The current player, especially a hypothetical player for example and didactic purposes. Compare: villain (“any opponent player”). Not to be confused with hero call (“a weak call against a supposed bluff”).", "tags": [], "examples": ["Let's discuss how to play if the hero has KK, and there's an ace on board."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(New York) A large sandwich made from meats and cheeses.", "tags": ["New York"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["hero sandwich", "more at submarine sandwich"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(film, photography, chiefly attributive) The product chosen from several candidates to be photograp